WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:09.899
Two students give the same wrong answer, for different reasons. Marks show what's wrong. Concept X-Ray shows why.

2
00:00:09.899 --> 00:00:17.344
A generic tutor says ‘incorrect’. Concept X-Ray names the misconception, finds its root cause, and alerts the teacher.

3
00:00:17.344 --> 00:00:24.813
It runs as a loop: diagnose, read the reasoning, update the learner model, target the next question, then schedule and report.

4
00:00:24.813 --> 00:00:33.762
The diagnostic covers both chapters. Each answer collects the option, a line of reasoning, and the student's confidence.

5
00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:43.957
Our student picks 0.25 amps and explains: ‘the first bulb uses up some of the current.’ They're certain.

6
00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:54.985
The X-Ray reads the reasoning, not just the answer. It names the misconception, quotes the evidence, and gives the fix.

7
00:00:54.985 --> 00:01:03.099
The learner model updates after every answer, using Bayesian Knowledge Tracing to separate real understanding from lucky guesses.

8
00:01:03.099 --> 00:01:11.224
After ten questions, the X-Ray has found four distinct misconceptions, each one backed by the student's own words.

9
00:01:11.224 --> 00:01:20.750
The concept graph shows the whole syllabus. Dashed purple rings mark root causes: weak foundations behind later mistakes.

10
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:28.700
Click any concept to see its mastery trend, prerequisites, active misconceptions, and next review date.

11
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:36.810
Practice targets the weakest concept, or its weaker prerequisite, at a difficulty matched to current mastery.

12
00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:45.258
Every decision is shown in the trace, so teachers can check the AI's choices step by step.

13
00:01:45.258 --> 00:01:53.452
A three-level hint ladder: nudge, trap warning, then method. Each hint lowers the mastery credit, so answers are earned.

14
00:01:53.452 --> 00:02:00.150
Students who work on paper can photograph their notebook. Gemini Vision reads the handwriting and diagnoses it.

15
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:08.269
SM-2 spaced repetition builds a review plan. Confident mistakes come back first, and mastered concepts are spaced out.

16
00:02:08.269 --> 00:02:17.739
Proof of learning: two clean answers close a misconception as Fixed. The teacher gets a before-and-after report.

17
00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:25.849
The teacher dashboard shows class-wide gaps: 31 students by 15 concepts, with the class average on the bottom row.

18
00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:34.545
Teachers see which wrong ideas are shared across the class, found from reasoning and not just scores.

19
00:02:34.545 --> 00:02:42.660
One click assigns a remedial set to exactly the students who share the misconception.

20
00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:52.115
The AI Lab measures the AI on held-out answers. This recording runs offline; the live site uses Gemini at concept-xray.vercel.app.

21
00:02:52.115 --> 00:02:58.533
Concept X-Ray: fix the reason, not just the answer.
